sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: B6 slot design (migration-dashboard/drafts/task-vm-slots.md, M1), docs/reference/compute-drivers.md (Task VM slots), docs/reference/node-provisioning.md, DECISIONS R1-R4.
  %% Tightened: flow-tighten rules 1, 3, 6, 9, 18, 20, 22 (the host work is one Ansible phase; the hub peer and the model key reuse the existing steps, the model key issued once by the workflow; one end check).
  %% status: reviewed
  %% command: none · enrol one task VM slot
  %% kind: task_vm.slot_enroll
  autonumber
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane H icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane HUB icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  %% lane VM icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>workflow execution
  participant H as Task VM host<br/>over ssh
  participant HUB as VPN hub<br/>over ssh
  participant VM as Slot VM<br/>task image
  Note over GW: Validate, record the slot
  %%> Started by:
  %%> - `node:update` when it raises the slot count of a task VM host, and the host-add flow
  %%> - there is no CLI command of its own; an operator runs `php artisan task-vms:enroll-slot HOST N` on the Gateway
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - the host is an active task VM host
  %%> - the reserved WireGuard range has a free address
  %%> - no other task holds the slot
  %%> Result:
  %%> - a slot row named `HOST-tvm-N`, state `provisioning`, with its WireGuard address, static bridge address and fixed MAC
  %%> - a Node with the `app-dev` role, the `pi-server` Process, a Pi token and a model key, made once and kept encrypted on the row
  %%> - a task is recorded with the full intent
  GW->>SW: Push the secrets<br/>vault: Pi token, model key
  %%> Why:
  %%> - secrets go Gateway → vault → step; the run inputs hold only vault key names
  %%> - the Gateway also pushes the model router credentials, as the model issue needs them
  %%> The model key:
  %%> - the Gateway makes and holds it, because the router teardown fence (`ai_router.keys_outstanding`) and the revoke at slot retire read it from the row
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-task-vm-slot-enroll
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - the slot name, host, project, pool and addresses
  %%> - the hub peer and the files of the identity tree, as text without secrets: the WireGuard config, the observer configuration and CA, the Pi unit with the name of the slot's Pi Process, and `models.json`
  %%> - the identity revision, and the pinned observer and Pi digests
  SW->>SW: Issue the model key<br/>workflow · task-vm-model-issue
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - registers the slot's model key with the model router; the key comes from the vault copy of the step above
  %%> - the key goes into the identity volume as part of `models.json`
  %%> Why first:
  %%> - the identity step below writes the key, so the router must know it before a VM can use it
  %%> Revoke:
  %%> - the key is revoked when the slot is retired, not when a task ends
  SW->>H: Create the identity<br/>ansible phase · identity
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - creates the volume `HOST-tvm-N-identity`
  %%> - makes the WireGuard key pair, the SSH host keys and the observer secret in a private temporary folder, and moves them into the volume
  %%> - writes the identity tree and `REVISION` from the vault Pi token and the model key of the step above
  %%> - prints only the WireGuard public key, the host key fingerprints and the sha256 of the observer secret
  %%> Why one phase:
  %%> - volume, keys and files are idempotent state with lists (rule 22)
  %%> Retry:
  %%> - a key or secret that exists is never made again, so a rerun keeps the slot identity
  %%> Fixed:
  %%> - the identity is written once and never rotated; the claim only checks `REVISION`
  %%> Not included:
  %%> - a private key never reaches Swamp, the Gateway or the vault
  SW->>HUB: Add the hub peer<br/>peer file · wg addconf
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - writes the slot's peer file from the public key of the identity step and reloads the hub
  %%> - the peer stays: a claim or a release never touches the hub
  %%> Idempotent:
  %%> - one step writes the peer file only when it differs; `wg addconf` accepts a peer it already has
  %%> - the peer list it prints is the read-back for the end check
  SW->>H: Start a proof VM<br/>workflow · task-vm-slot-boot
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - runs the same boot steps as a claim: remove a stale VM and seed clone, clone the seed, create the VM with the identity volume, start it, wait for the guest
  %%> - the instance user-data sets `ssh_deletekeys: false`, so cloud-init cannot replace the slot host keys, whatever the order of cloud-init and the identity unit
  %%> - a VM or clone left by an earlier attempt is never reused
  %%> Why:
  %%> - the slot counts as enrolled only when a VM with this identity comes up
  SW->>VM: Check the slot VM<br/>ssh exec · pinned host key
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - waits until `orbit-slot-identity.service` has finished (`systemctl is-active`), then runs one command
  %%> - the observer and Pi binaries match their pinned digests
  %%> - the observer answers, and Pi answers its capabilities probe
  %%> - the SSH host key equals the one the identity step printed
  %%> Why:
  %%> - the Incus agent answers about 4 s before the unit finishes, so it is not the signal
  SW->>H: Delete the proof VM<br/>ssh exec · incus delete
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - deletes the VM and its seed clone
  %%> - keeps the identity volume
  %%> When:
  %%> - it runs also when the boot or the check failed, so a failed run leaves no proof VM behind
  Note over SW: Check the slot<br/>assert
  %%> End check:
  %%> - a native `assert` over the step results
  %%> - the volume holds the expected `REVISION`
  %%> - the hub lists the peer
  %%> - the proof VM passed, and the VM and seed clone are gone
  alt every step passes
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
    %%> How the Gateway learns it:
    %%> - its run reader sees the terminal event; Swamp never calls the Gateway
    Note over GW: Record result
    %%> Result:
    %%> - records the WireGuard public key, the SSH host key, the observer digest and the identity revision
    %%> - the Node becomes `Active`
    %%> - the slot becomes `free`
    %%> - the task succeeds
  else a step fails
    H--xSW: exit ≠ 0
    %%> When:
    %%> - a host command, the hub reload, the model issue, the proof VM or the end check fails
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
    Note over GW: Mark the slot failed
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the slot is `failed`, so no claim can take it; the failed Operation is the signal, and no alert fires
    %%> - the task fails
    %%> On the host:
    %%> - the volume, the hub peer and the keys stay; there is no rollback
    %%> - the proof VM and its seed clone are deleted; one left by a crash is removed by the next boot, and the sweep does not report slot names as strays
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - run the enrolment again after fixing the cause; it keeps the keys and skips finished steps
  end
